body:
DTS build fails with 3 TypeScript errors due to type mismatches between hand-written Zod v4 type stubs and actual Zod v4 types.

- **`error-map.zod.ts`**: Replace hand-written `ObjectStackRawIssue` interface with `z.core.$ZodRawIssue` type alias — the manual interface had drifted from Zod v4 on `path` (`PropertyKey[]` vs `(string | number)[]`), `maximum` (`number | bigint` vs `number`), etc. Also widen `ZodIssueMinimal.path` to `PropertyKey[]`.

- **`stack.zod.ts`**: `hook.object` is `string | string[]` per `hook.zod.ts`, but `validateCrossReferences` passed it directly to `Set.has()`. Normalize to array before iterating:

```typescript
const hookObjects = Array.isArray(hook.object) ? hook.object : [hook.object];
for (const obj of hookObjects) {
  if (!objectNames.has(obj)) { ... }
}
```

